{
  "global": {
    "enabled": true,
    "densityMultiplier": 1.0
  },
  "landingPopulation": {
    "rule": "B1123 (#443) + B1161 (#480): a spell with NO spellsnew.eff record lands the style (impact + spellComplete), and that style landing plus its own held Source peaks at half the platform pool (constrained_presets.json spellParticlePool), so two overlapping no-record landings fit; the rates below give its schedule and SpellEffectsConfig::applyPool scales them to the peak. A spell WITH a record draws its slots' FILE populations (B1149) and the rule scales none of them: the oracle's pool (EQGraphicsDX9 -- per-emitter rings, ring full drops the rest of the frame's emission, 0x10061180) is a cap, not a scaler, and fable applies that rule at its one pool (new particles dropped while it is full: allocateParticle returns -1, sim_particles.cpp:774, sized from this config at renderer_sim_bridge.cpp:470). The largest record field a class-level 1-60 spell draws is record 35's (spellsnew.eff 104, spell 253): 3746 + 1168 = 4914 peak live (each slot's burst + perTick x tps x min(window, L), summed: an upper bound) -- inside the desktop 8192, over the sbc 4096 by 818, where the pool fills and drops. No count is scaled (refactor/B1149/README.md sec. 4; pinned by SpellPoolRule in tests/test_spell_colour_and_overrides.cpp and SpellLandingPool in tests/test_spell_landing_volume.cpp)."
  },
  "sourceRecords": {
    "rule": "B1153 (#473): the survey's per-record measured rows are retired -- every record is drawn by its spellsnew.eff record's EDD emitters (spellsnew.edd +0xA8 shape, +0xB8..+0xC0 offsets, +0xC4/+0xC8 tilts; B1149 population/sprite, B1150 shape, B1151 motion) and the measured values are regression bands in the tests/spell_fx_*_oracle.h headers (the generator: refactor/B1153/scripts/gen_row_bands.py, run against the pre-retirement config at e83a097d). What the file keeps is the NO-RECORD fallback: a spell whose field 145 is absent draws `default` (the style's body cloud on the caster, the B1130 median onset, B1122's holds), scaled by `scale`.",
    "scale": {
      "anchorAboveFeet": 3.6,
      "why": "B1120's entity anchor 3.6 world units above the feet; the retired row geometry's H 6.5 and 3.0 rad/s orbit (B1122's record-23 orbit, the 54/656 castGlow override) are the bands' kCasterHeight / kOrbitAngularVelocity in tests/spell_fx_row_oracle.h"
    },
    "default": {
      "anchor": "body",
      "onset": 0.41,
      "holdOther": 4.0,
      "holdSelf": 0.33
    },
    "defaultWhy": "A spell with no spellsnew.eff record (field 145 = 0) draws this row: the style's own body cloud (B1122) on the caster, from the B1130 median onset, holding B1122's measured holds past OP_Action (holdOther with another target, holdSelf on the caster). A spell that HAS a record holds the cast-animation term (EQ::kSpellFxCastAnimationSeconds, B1148) past OP_Action -- in code (sourceHold), not here: that is the 4.35 s hold every retired row carried. B1153 (#473): the per-record measured rows (anchor classes, holds, shapes) were the test seam's readers only; they are the bands in tests/spell_fx_row_oracle.h."
  },
  "targetRecords": {
    "rule": "B1153 (#473): the survey's per-record measured rows are retired -- every record lands as its spellsnew.eff record's Target stage (spellsnew.edd +0xA8 shape, +0xB8..+0xC0 offsets, +0xC4/+0xC8 tilts, depth +0xD0, +0x19C scale; B1149 population/sprite, B1150 shape, B1151 motion, B1152 the missile arrival) and the measured anchor classes and extents are regression bands in tests/spell_fx_row_oracle.h and tests/spell_fx_shape_oracle.h (the generator: refactor/B1153/scripts/gen_row_bands.py). What the file keeps is the NO-RECORD fallback: a spell whose field 145 is absent lands the style's own volume (spellComplete + impact) on the target's entity (`default`).",
    "default": {
      "anchor": "body"
    },
    "defaultWhy": "A spell with no spellsnew.eff record (field 145 = 0) lands the style volume on the target's entity (the B1120 volume on the target). B1153: the survey's per-record anchors (record 5's head/face, 16/28's feet/ground, 3's column, 27/40/... 's caster) were honored as placement classes; they are the bands' evidence, and the record spells that drew them take their placement from the file."
  },
